Subject: [PATCH 06/11] fix(strands): start the agent span before the
 structured-output tool and end a cancelled cycle span with the error

---
 .rust-port/staging/p10fixa/dispositions.md    |  3 +
 strands-rs/strands/src/agent/run.rs           | 20 ++++++-
 .../src/telemetry/tests/agent_tracer.rs       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 79 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixa/dispositions.md b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixa/dispositions.md
index 66fc4417a..6173dee36 100644
--- a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixa/dispositions.md
+++ b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixa/dispositions.md
@@ -10,3 +10,6 @@
 | parity-5 | Fixed: under `gen_ai_span_attributes_only`/Langfuse `start_search` no longer sets `content`; `end_search` (new `query` parameter) sets it once: the results, or the query when the search failed. Tests `telemetry::tests::tracer_methods::memory_spans::{a_memory_search_span_ends_with_one_content_attribute_when_opted_in, records_the_memory_search_query_as_a_span_attribute_and_skips_the_event_when_opted_in}` (the second now ends the span with an error). A search span dropped without `end_search` has no `content`. | this commit |
 | correctness-6 | Fixed: `LocalTracer::record_start` skips a start attribute (operation, provider, agent name/id, model, tools, tool definitions, system prompt, cycle id, tool name/call id, `name`) when a trace attribute has its key, and `record_trace_attributes` skips the keys a span sets after its start (`keys::SET_AFTER_START`: start/end time, usage, request duration, tool status/arguments/result, Langfuse type, `otel.status_*`), so each key is exported once with the TS winner. Test `telemetry::tests::tracer_methods::a_trace_attribute_replaces_a_start_attribute_and_an_end_attribute_replaces_it`. Known gap: a trace attribute named like a set-after-start key is dropped also on a span that never sets that key (TS keeps it there). | this commit |
 | parity-4 | Fixed: same change as correctness-6. | this commit |
+| parity-1 | Fixed: `run_pass` starts the agent span before it registers the structured-output tool (and ends the span with the error if the registration fails), so `gen_ai.agent.tools` never lists `strands_structured_output`. Test `telemetry::tests::agent_tracer::agent_span_tools_exclude_the_structured_output_tool`. | this commit |
+| parity-3 | Fixed: the cycle span ends with `Agent invocation cancelled` for `Stop::Cancelled` and with the TS `InterruptError` text (`Interrupt raised: <name>` / `<n> interrupts raised: <names>`) for `Stop::Interrupted`. Test `telemetry::tests::agent_tracer::ends_the_loop_span_with_an_error_when_the_invocation_is_cancelled_mid_model_call`; the interrupt arm has no test. | this commit |
+| correctness-7 | For the lead: not fixed. `execute_background` gets a `ToolAgent`, which has no telemetry handle, so the agent's `trace_attributes` have to travel `Agent` -> `background_tasks::ToolRun` -> `BackgroundToolRun` (`types/agent.rs`, `background_tasks/`, outside this track). Recommended: add `trace_attributes: Vec<(String, AttributeValue)>` to `ToolRun` and `BackgroundToolRun`, filled where the scheduler builds the run from the agent (a new `LocalTracer::trace_attributes()` getter), and call `telemetry.lock().tracer.set_trace_attributes(..)` on the run's `LocalTelemetry` in `tools/executors/executor.rs` before the `ToolTerminal` is built; extend the DIVERGENCES row at `docs/DIVERGENCES.md:79` until then. | - |
diff --git a/strands-rs/strands/src/agent/run.rs b/strands-rs/strands/src/agent/run.rs
index 31becb028..696b59138 100644
--- a/strands-rs/strands/src/agent/run.rs
+++ b/strands-rs/strands/src/agent/run.rs
@@ -443,11 +443,16 @@ impl Agent {
             tool: schema.map(StructuredOutputTool::new),
             choice: None,
         };
+        // Before the structured-output tool is registered, as in TS: the span doesn't list it.
+        self.start_agent_span(&input.messages);
         if let Some(tool) = &structured.tool {
-            self.local.tool_registry_mut().add(Arc::new(tool.clone()))?;
+            if let Err(error) = self.local.tool_registry_mut().add(Arc::new(tool.clone())) {
+                let outcome = Err(error.into());
+                self.end_agent_span(&outcome);
+                return outcome;
+            }
             self.structured_output_registered = true;
         }
-        self.start_agent_span(&input.messages);
         let outcome = self.cycles(input, state, hooks, out, &mut structured).await;
         self.end_agent_span(&outcome);
         if structured.tool.is_some() {
@@ -500,9 +505,18 @@ impl Agent {
             {
                 let mut telemetry = self.local.telemetry().lock();
                 telemetry.meter.end_cycle(started);
+                // TS closes the cycle with whatever error leaves it, a cancel or an interrupt too.
                 let error = match &cycle {
                     Err(Stop::Failed(error)) => Some(error.to_string()),
-                    _ => None,
+                    Err(Stop::Cancelled) => Some(CancelledError.to_string()),
+                    Err(Stop::Interrupted(interrupts)) => Some(match interrupts.as_slice() {
+                        [interrupt] => format!("Interrupt raised: {}", interrupt.name()),
+                        all => {
+                            let names: Vec<&str> = all.iter().map(Interrupt::name).collect();
+                            format!("{} interrupts raised: {}", all.len(), names.join(", "))
+                        }
+                    }),
+                    Ok(_) => None,
                 };
                 telemetry.tracer.end_cycle(error.as_deref());
             }
